<html>
<head>
	<title></title>
</head>
<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">
<p>Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
&nbsp;</p>

<p>Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},</p>

<p>Thank you for reaching out to the Qantas Customer Care team regarding your refund.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>If refund has been processed, use:</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>Your refund is on its way</strong><br />
Your refund has been processed and you should see the amount appear in your <em><strong>&lt;nominated account/credit card&gt;</strong></em> within 4 weeks. Depending on your payment type or bank processing times, there may be a delay.<br />
<br />
<strong><em>If refund has not been processed within 4 weeks due to large volume of requests, use:</em></strong><br />
<br />
<strong>Your refund is in progress</strong><br />
We understand that the delay in receiving your refund is frustrating and are doing our best to work through the large volume of requests as quickly as possible.<br />
<br />
You’ll receive an email confirmation once your request has been actioned. The expected processing time is approximately <em><strong>&lt;X days/weeks&gt;</strong></em>.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>If refund has not been processed after 4 weeks, use:</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>We’re looking into it</strong><br />
We understand that the delay in receiving your refund is frustrating. I can see that your request has been actioned by our team and funds were scheduled to be processed.<br />
<br />
As you haven’t received your refund, please contact your bank first. If they are unable to locate it within 4 weeks, I’ll investigate this and provide you with an update within <strong><em>&lt;X days&gt;</em></strong>.<br />
<br />
Thank you for your patience and understanding.</p>
</body>
</html>